      "name": "Antigravity",
      "defaultModel": "gemini-3.8-flash",
      "source": "Live POST https://daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com/v1internal:fetchAvailableModels read with the credential the Antigravity CLI (agy 1.1.18) owns, 2026-09-03, reported defaultAgentModelId gemini-3.8-flash-high and a 1,048,576-token window for all three Gemini 3.8 Flash rungs; reconfirmed 2026-10-18. Gemini 4 Argon replaces the previous Pro lineup on 2026-10-18: live agy 1.4.1 --model gemini-4-argon-{low,medium,high} --effort {low,medium,high} --print turns each exited 0 with the requested echo response using the same subscription credential and daily endpoint. The agy log showed gemini-4-argon-low sent as the wire model id, display name Gemini 4 Argon (Low), and project default-cli-project. Argon uses the three id-encoded effort rungs, not thinkingConfig. The backend gates Argon on client identity: the same fetch read with Fleet's previous antigravity/ide/2.5.5 User-Agent omits Argon and its turns 404, while agy 1.4.1's antigravity/cli/1.4.1 identity (which Fleet now sends) lists all three Argon rungs with a 1,048,576-token window, thinkingLevel 1/2/3, and defaultAgentModelId gemini-4-argon-medium. providerModelId selects the medium rung following that upstream default; omitted request effort still follows the existing resolver default. The codename-suffixed Gemini 4 Argon resolves downward to standard under the naming grammar, consistently with the same vendor model on Cursor. Claude and GPT-OSS models are served by the same subscription but are deliberately not exposed here.",
